# Treat binary assets as binary so autocrlf never rewrites their bytes.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mov binary

# Scripts that open with a shebang must stay LF in the WORKING TREE, not just
# in the index. Git stores them LF and hands Windows CRLF, and vitest's module
# loader does not treat a CRLF-terminated shebang line as a shebang: it leaves
# the # in code position, and the import dies with
# `SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token`.
#
# Isolated 2026-09-06 by bisection: shebang+LF imports fine, shebang+CRLF does
# not, and the em dashes in the same file were a red herring. CI never saw it
# because a Linux runner checks out LF, so this only ever broke Windows.
scripts/*.mjs text eol=lf
scripts/*.sh text eol=lf
